IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- LAYER 1, regulations 8 and 9 (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds
-- (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017, S.I. 2017/692, United Kingdom).  The text is a
-- plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text, and nothing
-- here is verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THE ANSWERS MEAN.  Every rule answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
--   JUST FALSE  the Regulations say no in their own words (the branch quotes the words).
--   NOTHING     the Regulations do not answer on these facts (the branch says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.  NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and
-- NOTHING (mlr1)", has the whole of it.

§ `Regulation 8 -- Application`

-- reg 8(2).  The list of persons to whom the Parts apply.  The core names the sixteen kinds a
-- relevant person can be (`Kind of relevant person`); paragraph (2) lists the first fifteen
-- (paragraph (c) names four kinds, paragraph (f) two) and says nothing of the auction platform,
-- which paragraph (3) deals with.  A kind that is not on the printed list is not "listed".
-- src:239 | (2) The persons listed in this paragraph are—
-- src:240 | (a) credit institutions;
-- src:241 | (b) financial institutions;
-- src:242 | (c) auditors, insolvency practitioners, external accountants and tax advisers;
-- src:243 | (d) independent legal professionals;
-- src:244 | (e) trust or company service providers;
-- src:245 | (f) estate agents and letting agents;
-- src:246 | (g) high value dealers;
-- src:247 | (h) casinos;
-- src:248 | (i) art market participants;
-- src:249 | (j) cryptoasset exchange providers;
-- src:250 | (k) custodian wallet providers.
@ref reg 8(2) (src:239-250)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(2) the kind of person is one of those listed in this paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `credit institution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `financial institution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `auditor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `insolvency practitioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `external accountant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `tax adviser` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `independent legal professional` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `trust or company service provider` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `estate agent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `letting agent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `high value dealer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `casino` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `art market participant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `cryptoasset exchange provider` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `custodian wallet provider` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `auction platform` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The persons listed in this paragraph are—" (an auction platform is not among (a) to (k); paragraph (3) treats it separately and the list is not closed with "only")

-- reg 8(1)(a).  "are listed in paragraph (2)": a person can be several kinds at once (a law firm can be
-- an independent legal professional and a trust or company service provider), so the
-- person is listed if any one of its kinds is.
-- src:236 | (1) Parts 1 to 6 , 7A and 8 to 11 apply to the persons (“relevant persons”) acting in the course of business carried on by them in the United Kingdom, who—
-- src:237 | (a) are listed in paragraph (2); and
-- src:238 | (b) do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15.
@ref reg 8(1)(a) (src:236-238)
GIVEN `the kinds of the person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(1)(a) the person is listed in paragraph (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN k YIELD `reg 8(2) the kind of person is one of those listed in this paragraph` k EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the kinds of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) are listed in paragraph (2)" (no kind of the person is on the list)

-- reg 8(1)(b).  Three-valued negation of the answer of reg 15: the person is outside the
-- exclusions if reg 15 says it does not come within them.
@ref reg 8(1)(b) (src:238-238)
GIVEN `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(1)(b) the person does not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 15 has not answered whether the person comes within its exclusions

-- reg 8(1).  Who the Parts apply to: a person acting in the course of business carried on in the
-- United Kingdom who is listed in paragraph (2) and is not excluded by regulation 15.
-- A person that is not all three is not a "relevant person" in the Regulations' sense.
-- SEAM S-7 and S-8 (answering): other parts take this answer as the input
-- `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`.
@ref reg 8(1) (src:236-238)
GIVEN `the kinds of the person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `acting in the course of business carried on by the person in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8 the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`acting in the course of business carried on by the person in the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the persons (“relevant persons”) acting in the course of business carried on by them in the United Kingdom"
        IF `reg 8(1)(a) the person is listed in paragraph (2)` `the kinds of the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who— (a) are listed in paragraph (2)"
        IF `reg 8(1)(b) the person does not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15` `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15"
        IF `reg 8(1)(b) the person does not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15` `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 15 has not answered whether the person comes within its exclusions

-- reg 8(3).  A regulation, as the Regulations number it: a number and, for a regulation such as 18A
-- or 52B, a letter suffix ("" for none).
DECLARE `reg 8(3) Regulation` HAS
    `number`        IS A NUMBER
    `letter suffix` IS A STRING

-- reg 8(3).  The regulations that apply to an auction platform.  The list is "3, 7, 9, 15, 17 to
-- 21, 24, 25, 46, 47, 50 to 52, 65 to 82, 84, 86 to 93, 101, 102 and 106".  A lettered regulation
-- (18A, 74A) lies inside a range when its number is below the range's last number; a lettered
-- regulation after the last number of a range (52A, 52B) or after a single number (46A) is not named
-- by the paragraph (fork F-8(3) in NOTES.md).
-- src:251 | (3) Regulations 3, 7, 9, 15, 17 to 21, 24, 25, 46, 47, 50 to 52, 65 to 82, 84, 86 to 93, 101, 102 and 106 apply to an auction platform acting in the course of business carried on by it in the United Kingdom, and such an auction platform is a relevant person for the purposes of those provisions.
@ref reg 8(3) (src:251-251)
GIVEN regulation IS A `reg 8(3) Regulation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(3) the regulation is one of those that apply to an auction platform` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF regulation's `letter suffix` EQUALS "" AND elem (regulation's `number`) (LIST 3, 7, 9, 15, 24, 25, 46, 47, 84, 101, 102, 106) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF regulation's `number` AT LEAST 17 AND regulation's `number` AT MOST 21 AND (regulation's `letter suffix` EQUALS "" OR regulation's `number` LESS THAN 21) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF regulation's `number` AT LEAST 50 AND regulation's `number` AT MOST 52 AND (regulation's `letter suffix` EQUALS "" OR regulation's `number` LESS THAN 52) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF regulation's `number` AT LEAST 65 AND regulation's `number` AT MOST 82 AND (regulation's `letter suffix` EQUALS "" OR regulation's `number` LESS THAN 82) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF regulation's `number` AT LEAST 86 AND regulation's `number` AT MOST 93 AND (regulation's `letter suffix` EQUALS "" OR regulation's `number` LESS THAN 93) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names the regulations that apply to an auction platform and says nothing of any other (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 8(3).  Who is a relevant person for a given regulation.  A person listed in paragraph (2) is one for
-- every regulation (reg 8(1)); an auction platform is one only "for the purposes of those provisions".
-- SEAM S-8 (answering, per regulation): the seat passes this answer, for the regulation it asks about, to every duty
-- as the input `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`.
@ref reg 8(3) (src:251-251)
GIVEN `the kinds of the person` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
      `acting in the course of business carried on by the person in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      regulation IS A `reg 8(3) Regulation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(3) the person is a relevant person for the purposes of the regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the kinds of the person` `acting in the course of business carried on by the person in the United Kingdom` `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (elem `auction platform` `the kinds of the person`) THEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the kinds of the person` `acting in the course of business carried on by the person in the United Kingdom` `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions`
        IF NOT (`acting in the course of business carried on by the person in the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an auction platform acting in the course of business carried on by it in the United Kingdom"
        IF `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15" (reg 8(1)(b), which paragraph (3) leaves in place)
        IF `reg 8(3) the regulation is one of those that apply to an auction platform` regulation EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 8(3) the regulation is one of those that apply to an auction platform` regulation EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulation 15 has not answered whether the auction platform comes within its exclusions
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an auction platform is a relevant person "for the purposes of those provisions" and the paragraph says nothing of any other regulation (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 8(3A).  Regulation 29 reaches the customer who is given a pooled account by a relevant person
-- ("pooled account" in the sense of reg 29(10)).
-- src:252 | (3A) Regulation 29 applies to a customer provided with a pooled account (within the meaning of paragraph (10) of that regulation) by a relevant person.
@ref reg 8(3A) (src:252-252)
GIVEN `the customer is provided with a pooled account by a relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(3A) regulation 29 applies to the customer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the customer is provided with a pooled account by a relevant person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph says regulation 29 applies "to a customer provided with a pooled account" and says nothing of any other customer

-- reg 8(4).  The definitions in regulations 10 to 14 apply for the purposes of regulation 8.
-- Regulation 14A (which is numbered after 14) carries its own "In these Regulations" and so reaches
-- regulation 8 by its own words; this paragraph names 10 to 14 only.
-- src:253 | (4) The definitions in regulations 10 to 14 apply for the purposes of this regulation.
@ref reg 8(4) (src:253-253)
GIVEN regulation IS A `reg 8(3) Regulation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(4) the definition in the regulation applies for the purposes of regulation 8` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF regulation's `letter suffix` EQUALS "" AND regulation's `number` AT LEAST 10 AND regulation's `number` AT MOST 14 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names "regulations 10 to 14"; a lettered regulation such as 14A, or any other regulation, is not named

§ `Helpers: three-valued OR and AND over the limbs of a list`

-- Helper, named for the list it was first needed for (reg 8(2): "The persons listed in this paragraph are— (a) ... (k)").
-- Used wherever the Regulations define a term by "means" followed by limbs joined by "or".  One limb that
-- answers JUST TRUE makes the whole TRUE; if every limb answers JUST FALSE the whole is FALSE; otherwise the
-- Regulations have not answered and the whole is NOTHING.  A caller must never read NOTHING as FALSE.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST TRUE) limbs THEN JUST TRUE
        IF all (GIVEN limb YIELD limb EQUALS JUST FALSE) limbs THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the limbs are the only ones the definition names ("means—") and every one answers no
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): at least one limb has not been answered and none holds

-- Helper, named for the conditions it was first needed for (reg 8(1): "who— (a) are listed ...; and (b) do not come within ...").
-- Every condition must hold.  One that answers JUST FALSE makes the whole FALSE; if every condition answers
-- JUST TRUE the whole is TRUE; otherwise NOTHING.
GIVEN conditions IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8(1) all of the conditions of the list hold` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN condition YIELD condition EQUALS JUST FALSE) conditions THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a condition joined by "and" is not met
        IF all (GIVEN condition YIELD condition EQUALS JUST TRUE) conditions THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): at least one condition has not been answered and none has failed

§ `Regulation 9 -- Carrying on business in the United Kingdom`

-- reg 9(3), the second case: the registered office (or, with none, the head office) is in the United
-- Kingdom and the day-to-day management of the business is the responsibility of that office or of another
-- establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom.
-- src:257 | (3) The second case is where—
-- src:258 | (a) A's registered office (or if A does not have a registered office, A's head office) is in the United Kingdom; and
-- src:259 | (b) the day-to-day management of the carrying on of A's business is the responsibility of—
-- src:260 | (i) that office, or
-- src:261 | (ii) another establishment maintained by A in the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 9(3) (src:257-261)
GIVEN `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` AND (`the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` OR `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second case is where— (a) ...; and (b) ..." (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; this function answers whether A is within the second case, and says nothing of A in the other cases: reg 9(1) still answers NOTHING for a person within no case; fork F-9)

-- reg 9(4), the third case: a casino providing facilities for remote gambling, with remote gambling
-- equipment in Great Britain or, with none there, the facilities used there.
-- src:262 | (4) The third case is where—
-- src:263 | (a) A is a casino which provides facilities for remote gambling (within the meaning of section 4 of the Gambling Act 2005 (remote gambling) ) and—
-- src:264 | (b) either—
-- src:265 | (i) at least one piece of remote gambling equipment (within the meaning of section 36(4) of the Gambling Act 2005 (territorial application)) is situated in Great Britain, or
-- src:266 | (ii) no such equipment is situated in Great Britain but the facilities provided by A are used there.
@ref reg 9(4) (src:262-266)
GIVEN `A is a casino which provides facilities for remote gambling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one piece of remote gambling equipment is situated in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no such equipment is situated in Great Britain but the facilities provided by A are used there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 9(4) the third case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `A is a casino which provides facilities for remote gambling` AND (`at least one piece of remote gambling equipment is situated in Great Britain` OR `no such equipment is situated in Great Britain but the facilities provided by A are used there`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third case is where— (a) ...; and (b) ..." (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; this function answers whether A is within the third case; fork F-9)

-- reg 9(5)(b).  For the second case, it does not matter where the person the business is carried on
-- with is situated.  The rule of reading is a function over where that person is: the answer of
-- reg 9(3) is the same for both places.
DECLARE `reg 9(5)(b) where the other party to the business is situated` IS ONE OF
    `reg 9(5)(b) in the United Kingdom`
    `reg 9(5)(b) outside the United Kingdom`

-- src:267 | (5) For the purposes of paragraph (3)—
-- src:268 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:269 | (b) it is irrelevant where the person with whom the business is carried on is situated.
@ref reg 9(5) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `where the person with whom the business is carried on is situated` IS A `reg 9(5)(b) where the other party to the business is situated`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 9(5)(b) the second case, whatever the situation of the person with whom the business is carried on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the person with whom the business is carried on is situated`
    WHEN `reg 9(5)(b) in the United Kingdom` THEN `reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom`
    WHEN `reg 9(5)(b) outside the United Kingdom` THEN `reg 9(3) the second case where A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` `A's registered office, or if A has none its head office, is in the United Kingdom` `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of that office` `the day-to-day management of A's business is the responsibility of another establishment A maintains in the United Kingdom`

-- reg 9(1).  A relevant person is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom in the cases the
-- regulation describes "even if A would not otherwise be regarded as doing so".  The first case, in
-- paragraph (2), is blank in the rendering.  The regulation adds cases; it does not take any away, so a
-- person that is not within a case and would not otherwise be regarded as carrying on business here is
-- not decided by it.
-- src:255 | (1) For the purposes of these Regulations, a relevant person (“A”) is to be regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom in the cases described in this regulation even if A would not otherwise be regarded as doing so.
@ref reg 9(1) (src:255-255)
GIVEN `A would otherwise be regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 9(3) the second case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 9(4) the third case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 9(1) A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `A would otherwise be regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 9(3) the second case` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 9(4) the third case` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the regulation says A is regarded as carrying on business in the United Kingdom "in the cases described in this regulation even if A would not otherwise be regarded as doing so" and says nothing of A in any other case

